        "phase": "BB7_RAF1_QC_JOIN",
        "label": "RAF1 Arm QC Join",
        "basic_block": "BB7",
        "compiler_label": "bsbbif_7_j",
        "notes": "Dispose all RAF1-arm signal droplets regardless of QC outcome. Mirrors BB4 for the RAF1 arm. Falls into BB8 (terminal).",
        "operations": [
          {
            "op": "dispose",
            "targets": ["signalRaf1","signalRaf2","signalRaf3","signalRaf4","signalRaf5","signalRaf6"]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "phase": "BB8_TERMINAL",
        "label": "Final Cleanup",
        "basic_block": "BB8",
        "compiler_label": "finalCleanup",
        "notes": "No instructions. Single exit node of the CFG. Compiler emits no additional DOT node since BB7 has no further operations after disposal.",
        "operations": []
      }
    ],

    "known_bugs_fixed": [
      {
        "fix_id": 1,
        "location": "Day-1 transfection-efficiency checkpoint, hoechstTfx* dispense calls",
        "original_error": "hoechstTfx* variables dispensed from manifest calceinAM instead of manifest hoechst",
        "impact": "Would have dispensed Calcein-AM (cytoplasmic esterase probe, lambda_em~450nm) instead of Hoechst 33342 (nuclear stain, lambda_em~461nm). CellProfiler transfection pipeline requires Hoechst to identify and count nuclei in Module 1; using Calcein-AM would produce invalid nuclear object detection and incorrect transfection efficiency measurements.",
        "fix": "manifest hoechst re-added to declarations; all 12 hoechstTfx* dispense calls changed from calceinAM to hoechst"
      },
      {
        "fix_id": 2,
        "location": "Day-3 Sorafenib serial dilution chain, variable reuse",
        "original_error": "Intermediate variables (drugConc120, drugConc60, etc.) were split in two separate sections of code — once in the dilution chain and again when allocating arm-specific aliquots — causing double-use of spent fluid variables",
        "impact": "BioScript compiler tracks fluid ownership; splitting an already-spent variable is a fluid-ownership violation that would cause a compiler error or incorrect graph generation",
        "fix": "Each dilution step now immediately produces three named outputs (_ctrlAliquot, _raf1Aliquot, _carry) from a single split sequence. The carry feeds the next step; the two aliquots go to the Ctrl and RAF1 arms. No variable is split more than once."
      }
    ]
  }
}
